+#### Limit exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or backed by, the same underlying currency (for example several BTC pairs, or several coins settled in the same stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several of your open trades at once.
+
+To cap this concentration risk, set `max_single_currency_exposure` to the maximum fraction of your total tradable capital (see [Tradable balance](#tradable-balance)) that may be committed, in aggregate, to open trades sharing the same underlying (base) currency - e.g. `0.3` allows at most 30% of your tradable capital to be tied up in BTC-denominated pairs (`BTC/USDT`, `BTC/USDT:USDT`, ...) at the same time, regardless of how many separate trades that spans.
+
+When opening (or increasing the size of) a trade would push the combined exposure to that pair's underlying currency above the configured limit, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit - or the trade is skipped entirely if even the exchange minimum stake can no longer be met. This applies identically whether the bot is trading live/dry-run or backtesting.
+
+```json
+"max_single_currency_exposure": 0.3,
+```
+
+!!! Note
+    This setting can be set in the configuration or in the strategy, [like other similar parameters](#parameters-in-the-strategy). It is disabled (no cap) by default.
+
 #### Amend last stake amount
 
 Assuming we have the tradable balance of 1000 USDT, `stake_amount=400`, and `max_open_trades=3`.
